      "content": "Taking old antibiotics prescribed for a different infection can be very dangerous for several reasons. Antibiotics must be the correct type for the bacteria causing your infection, and improper use can lead to resistant infections. Because of the risk involved, do not take any old medication and please seek advice from a medical professional.",
